Here's a concrete Terraform example for implementing CCPA opt-out blocking logic in AWS. This creates a complete solution that automatically denies data access to opted-out users.

## Architecture Overview
- **IAM Policy**: Denies access to S3/Redshift/DynamoDB for opted-out users
- **Lambda Function**: Processes opt-out requests and updates IAM policy
- **DynamoDB Table**: Stores opted-out user IDs
- **API Gateway**: Exposes endpoint for opt-out requests

## Terraform Code

```hcl
# main.tf

terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.0"
  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source  = "hashicorp/aws"
      version = "~> 5.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2" # Change to your region
}

# ============================================
# 1. DynamoDB Table for Opted-Out Users
# ============================================
resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "ccpa_opt_out" {
  name         = "ccpa-opt-out-users"
  billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key     = "user_id"

  attribute {
    name = "user_id"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "opt_out_date"
    type = "S"
  }

  global_secondary_index {
    name            = "opt_out_date_index"
    hash_key        = "opt_out_date"
    projection_type = "ALL"
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "CCPA Opt-Out Users"
    Compliance  = "CCPA"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

